2. Missing Authorization Checks (IDOR)
The critical vulnerability is Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR).  When you request a profile, the server performs the following logic:

Extract Hash: Takes the hash from the URL.
Lookup: Finds the user profile associated with that hash. 
Display: Shows the profile content.
What is missing? The server never checks if the currently logged-in user (Guest, ID 3000) has permission to view the requested profile.  It blindly trusts that if you have the correct hash, you are authorized to see the data. 

