4. Why Hashing Failed as a Control
Hashing is a one-way function designed for integrity and password storage, not for access control tokens in URLs. 

Feature	Vulnerable Implementation (Hashgate)	Secure Implementation
Identifier	Sequential Integer (3000, 3001)	Random UUID (550e8400-e29b...)
Access Control	Possession of Hash (MD5(ID))	Server-side Session Validation
Logic	"If hash matches, show data."	"If User A is logged in, can they see User B?"
Result	Trivial Brute-force	Impossible to guess

